concerns over low water levels at lake  mead making headlines today thank you  for staying with us here at 4 30 i'm  kirsten joyce and i'm christian casadas  well there has been so much discussion  about the colorado river and the water  levels in lake mead on wednesday the  water level mark sat at  1049 feet and one month ago it was at  1042 feet now the increase is all due to  the recent storms and you can see just  how far the colorado river stretches  among the seven states here including of  course ours that's right well one  non-profit group says that our problem  here for our water situation all comes  from an antique plumbing at the glen  canyon dam which is just lake uh near  lake powell  and now it's time to come up with a  solution to combat the water supply  crisis that's right  the system needs flexibility and it  needs flexibility now environmental  advocates sounding the alarm on the  water supply crisis from the colorado  river which impacts lake mead and  southern nevada residents the bureau of  reclamation  unveiled the call to congress  for the seven basin states to come up  with a plan within just 60 days to cut  between two and four million acre feet  of water from the colorado river basin  zachary frankel is the executive  director for the utah rivers council he  says the water problem stems from old  plumbing at the glen canyon dam near  lake powell  even though someone in las vegas might  not know anything or care much about  what's happening at glen canyon dams the  problem is  that the antique plumbing inside glen  canyon dam is has the potential to  prevent  las vegas and nevada from getting its  full water supply out of the colorado  river now a coalition of several  agencies is recommending two possible  solutions either whitening or drill  additional tubes to increase the water  flow or construct new bypass tunnels to  rise the river level once the water  level starts dropping another 45 feet  we're going to have major water supply  delivery problems  to 30 million people it's unclear how  much the repair cost would be but frank  hell and the coalition want congress to  fund a study soon before it's too late  this really should have happened five  years  ago well the bureau of reclamation's  deadline for all seven states including  nevada is on august 15th now if the  states do not identify a plan to cut  water use the bureau says it will use  its authority to impose huge water cuts  on all the states now also be on the  lookout for this flyer right here in  your mailbox the southern nevada water  authority wants to remind all residents  about the water situation at lake mead
 

